{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And they shall eat the flesh at night.</b> At the hour when all people are found in their houses." "<b>On this night.</b> On the night of the fifteenth of Nisan, which is that very night of the new moon that I am speaking with you now." "<b>Roast with fire.</b> So that its scent goes and wafts to the nostrils of the Egyptians, and they will know that you are eating their object of dread." "<b>Upon bitter herbs.</b> With bitter herbs — all of this is a way of disgrace, that they should eat it with something bad and bitter and not with something prestigious and sweet."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {2 "Reading יראתם (their fear/dread) as written; the word may carry the sense of 'that which they fear' or 'their abomination.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:06.895297473Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}